  "ref": "JOS.3.12",
  "review_notes": [
    "The ASV renders the doubled אִישׁ אֶחָד once, as every ... a man: every goes to the first אֶחָד as the distributive numeral (rule 41), a man to the first אִישׁ, and the second pair is unrepresented under rule 22. Giving the first pair the unrepresented status and the second the English was the competing reading; nothing in the ASV's order settles it, and first-realized is the ordinary treatment of a repeated element."
